    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d103">

                <pb facs="0104" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg98"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/1933: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief, United States Asiatic
                        Fleet</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hart</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chief of Naval
                        Operations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stark</hi>)<anchor n="94" xml:id="d103-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-10-22">October 22, 1939</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am still of the opinion that my preparations are fully sufficient to meet the
                    present conditions although the difficulties of patrol have been increased in
                    the extra-Settlement roads sector because of the shooting that occurred there
                    recently. I do not consider it wise to incorporate our marines with other
                    Settlement troops. Increased uneasiness among citizens of the United States
                    residing here may be caused by the British; however, the British do not seem to
                    be as greatly alarmed as the Americans.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
